    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.08) and **Yordan Alvarez** (80.06). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Arrighetti and a generous stolen base environment; his elite sprint speed gives him a unique profile that offsets the minor wind resistance. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start staple, as his elite 0.421 xwOBA provides the necessary firepower to anchor the heart of our order despite a stiff wind blowing in. **Colt Keith** (69.64) and **Junior Caminero** (69.34) also provide strong returns, with **Colt Keith**\u2019s lead-off spot against Chris Bassitt providing a significant efficiency boost that overrides the risk of Bassitt\u2019s experienced arsenal.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin**, who fell just shy of the threshold with a 44.97 score. While **Caleb Durbin** maintains the profile of a late-game stolen base specialist, his projected #9 spot in the order and a tough matchup against Connor Prielipp hampered his daily efficiency, leading us to favor the higher-probability output of **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**. We are also keeping a close watch on **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and the rest of the bottom half of the order, as their \"Lineup Pending\" status necessitates a conservative approach to game caps. Risks remain prevalent, particularly with **Christian Yelich** facing a tough 3.50 xERA arm in Justin Wrobleski, and we are monitoring the wind reports at the venues for **Yordan Alvarez** and **Junior Caminero** closely, as the inward flow could suppress power numbers if exit velocities don't reach the upper quartile.",
